--- body ---
## Context

Child 2 of tracker 1226. Switches the pre-merge gate to the cheap set once
child 1244's runner tests main after every merge. This is the latency win:
a gate record runs 88 to 95 s today, `make lint` 6 to 15 s (padme, READ).

Author ruling, 2026-10-27: **`/verify-gate` does not run the full suite
before the merge** — "it is the whole point". Adherence stays before the merge
through `make lint` (`pytest -m adherence`).

## Design

- `.merge-gate.json` declares a before set (ticket validator, agnostic and
  pipefail guards, catalog drift, `make lint`) and an after set (the full
  declared set, test suite included). Read from main, as today.
- The `tiers` key goes: every merge runs the cheap set, so the bookkeeping
  subset adds nothing. Delete `effective()` / `accepted_scopes()`
  tier handling in `scripts/merge-gate.py`; keep the `tier`
  subcommand, which still decides whether a PR needs `/gaze`.
- `/verify-gate` check plan (`skills/verify-gate/SKILL.md` § Check
  plan, `merge-gate.py plan`) covers only the before set; its
  `unresolved_adherence_violations` reads the `make lint` check, not
  `pytest-guard`. The `rerun` key follows: keep it only if it still
  selects within the before set.
- Guard hook (`hooks/reference-transaction`) and `scripts/main_sweep.py`
  accept a merge carrying a passing before-merge record.
- `skills/merge/SKILL.md` states the two moments in one place (§ Gating
  tiers as it stands after 1225).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `.merge-gate.json` declares the before-merge and after-merge check sets; the before set holds no test-suite run; the `tiers` key and its code path are gone.
- [ ] A merge records the before set on its candidate and lands; measured end to end with the `step_clock.py` duration line, against today's record (88 to 95 s).
- [ ] `/verify-gate` runs no full suite before the merge; its adherence finding reads the `make lint` check.
- [ ] The guard hook and the audit accept a main whose merges carry a before-merge record; `skills/merge/SKILL.md` states the two moments in one place.
- [ ] The harness gate passes.

## Raid annotation (Imagine+Plan, 2026-10-27)
- **Premise.** Holds, no PREMISE-OBJECTION. Tree today: `.merge-gate.json` carries `tiers` and `rerun`; `merge-gate.py` has `effective()` (l.244, called by `cmd_run`) and `accepted_scopes()` (l.253, called by `decide` callers and `main_sweep._verdict` l.75); `pytest-guard` = `make check-tests` (full suite); `make lint` = `pytest -m adherence` exists (Makefile l.31) but is not a declared check. 1244 adds `run-after`, an after-merge scope suffix and an audit pass; it leaves `tiers`/`effective` alone. The Blocked-by 1244 is real: dropping the suite before the merge while nothing tests main would leave main untested.
- **1236 overlap: none, no overtaking.** 1236 is about `BOOKKEEPING` (merge-gate.py l.82) not listing `tickets/reviews/`, so `tier --since` answers `full` after seat reports are recorded. 1245 keeps the `tier` subcommand and `BOOKKEEPING` verbatim (its own text says so) and only removes the record-content tier. The review-voiding trap fires in `tier`, which stays. Side effect to note: after 1245 a bookkeeping candidate no longer needs the suite, so a re-gate after the close commit costs seconds, but 1236's criteria 1 to 3 still stand untouched. Both edit `scripts/merge-gate.py` (different functions) and 1236 maybe `skills/merge/SKILL.md` Gating tiers: serialize or rebase.
- **Simplest path.** Keep `checks` as the full (after) set, which 1244's runner already reads. Add one key `"before": [names]` (subset of `checks`), plus a new check `{"name": "lint", "argv": ["make","lint"]}`; `before` = validate-tickets, agnostic-guard, pipefail-guard, skills-drift, lint. Replace `effective()` with `before_set(config)` (checks filtered by `before`, scope `<scope>/before-merge`, mirroring 1244's `/after-merge`); `accepted_scopes` collapses to one scope per moment; delete the `tiers` validation block (l.359-367) and the tier branch of `cmd_run`. Gate-on-gate: `cmd_check`/hook/audit use `scope_line(before_set(...))`, with no candidate-diff argument any more (`effective` needed `base, oid`; the signature simplifies). Antipattern scan: no new schema beyond one list; no second config file (the ticket title says "split .merge-gate.json", one file with two sets is the minimal reading, flag if the author wants two files); do not keep `rerun` unless it selects within `before`: all five before checks cost under 15 s together, so re-running them all on a bookkeeping delta is cheaper than the key, and `cmd_plan` (l.615) then drops the `rerun` read. Recommend deleting `rerun` and its validation (keeps the `reuse` rule for an empty delta). If the author keeps it, it shrinks to `validate-tickets, agnostic-guard`.
- **Actions.** (1) failing test; (2) `.merge-gate.json`: add `lint`, `before`, delete `tiers`, `rerun`, fix `about`; (3) `scripts/merge-gate.py`: items above and the docstring "Gating tiers" paragraph (l.26-33) reduced to the `tier` subcommand; (4) `scripts/main_sweep.py` l.75 and `hooks/reference-transaction` comment l.26-30 and its test; (5) `skills/verify-gate/SKILL.md` l.59 and § Check plan l.153-165 (adherence = `lint` check; drop the `rerun` paragraph); (6) `skills/merge/SKILL.md` § Gating tiers: one place naming before and after; (7) measure with `step_clock.py` before/after on padme (criterion 2).
- **Files.** `.merge-gate.json`, `scripts/merge-gate.py`, `scripts/main_sweep.py`, `hooks/reference-transaction` (comments), `skills/merge/SKILL.md`, `skills/verify-gate/SKILL.md`, `tests/test_merge_gate.py`, `tests/test_merge_gate_plan.py`, `tests/test_main_sweep.py` (l.264 plants `tiers`), `tests/test_main_guard_hook.py`, `tests/test_gating_tiers_home.py`, `docs/2026-10-21-main-update-guard.md` if it names tiers.
- **First failing test** (`tests/test_merge_gate.py`): temp repo with a config of two checks, `slow` (`false`) and `fast` (`true`), `"before": ["fast"]`; `merge-gate run` exits 0, the note lists only `fast` under scope `S/before-merge`, and `check` passes while a config still carrying `"tiers"` now fails `load_config`. Not tautological: the `slow` check is a failing command, so a runner that ignores `before` goes red; run the real script on a real temp repo, no mock of `load_config`. Second test: the repo's own `.merge-gate.json` has a `before` set containing `lint` and none of `pytest-guard`.
- **Interaction with 1244's PR.** Both touch `scripts/merge-gate.py` (1244 adds `run-after`, an after scope; 1245 rewrites `effective`/`accepted_scopes`/`cmd_run`/`load_config`), `scripts/main_sweep.py` (1244 audit pass; 1245 l.75), `skills/merge/SKILL.md` (step 8 vs § Gating tiers), `tests/test_main_sweep.py`, `docs/2026-10-21-main-update-guard.md`. Hard sequencing: start 1245 only on main after 1244 merges, then rebase; contract with 1244 to confirm now: its runner reads the after set from `checks` unchanged, and `accepted_scopes` stays a tuple function so 1245 can narrow it. 1244's red-ticket PR rides the bookkeeping tier today (runs `pytest-guard`, deadlock noted in 1244's feasibility); after 1245 its before-record is the cheap set, which removes that deadlock, so the split-off red-ticket child should be blocked by 1245, not by 1244.
- **Ticket 1247** edits only the top IDH_ROOT paragraph of skills (`skills/merge/SKILL.md` l.15 and `skills/verify-gate/SKILL.md` head). 1245 edits other sections of those two files: textual merge is clean, no semantic interaction. Rebase before the gate.
- **Risk.** (a) The cheap set loses coverage of `test_merge_gate*` itself on a PR that edits the gate: the after-runner catches it only after main moves (the intended Trust, Verify, Monitor trade, but state it in the PR). (b) `make lint` name collision with the after-set `pytest-guard` (runs adherence twice there): harmless, or drop `lint` from `checks` and keep it only in `before`, which is not allowed as `before` is a subset; accept the duplicate.
